From: Zinwa Q25 port <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: dsi: program video timing on bootloader handoff

When LK leaves DSI0 running in video mode, mtk_dsi_poweron() keeps the whole
DSI/D-PHY state, including LK's porch word counts. LK sizes those for 60 fps
at a slower link than the 652 Mbps it actually runs, so the Q25 panel scanned
out at 73.5 Hz while the DRM mode said 60 Hz: compositor/GTK frame pacing then
stalls and catches up periodically.

Keep the running PHY, but recompute the PHY timing for the link rate implied
by the mode and program the video timing from the mode. The panel mode must
use a pixel clock matching LK's link rate (panel-q20: 54.333 MHz, stretched
HFP for 60 Hz).

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
index 580fc8233..0b6a0638b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -711,6 +711,21 @@ static int mtk_dsi_poweron(struct mtk_dsi *dsi)
 			       dsi->regs + dsi->driver_data->reg_shadow_dbg_off);
 		writel(0, dsi->regs + DSI_INTEN);
 		writel(0, dsi->regs + DSI_INTSTA);
+		/*
+		 * Keep the bootloader's running D-PHY, but take over the video
+		 * timing. The bootloader sizes its porches for a slower link than
+		 * the one it actually runs (the vendor kernel stretches them
+		 * later), so left alone the panel scans out faster than the mode
+		 * we advertise (73.5 Hz instead of 60 on the Zinwa Q25). The mode's
+		 * pixel clock must match the bootloader's link rate.
+		 */
+		ret = mipi_dsi_pixel_format_to_bpp(dsi->format);
+		if (ret > 0 && dsi->vm.pixelclock) {
+			dsi->data_rate = DIV_ROUND_UP_ULL(dsi->vm.pixelclock * ret,
+							  dsi->lanes);
+			mtk_dsi_phy_timconfig(dsi);
+			mtk_dsi_config_vdo_timing(dsi);
+		}
 		dsi->lanes_ready = true;
 		dsi->enabled = true;
 		return 0;
